Merits
Reduced Cost: It is more economical than the census technique as the task of
collection and analysis of data is confined only to a fraction of the population.
Greater speed: In this method, only representative units are approached.
Smaller volume of data saves time not only in collecting the information, but
also in the processing, editing and analysing the data.
Greater accuracy: When sampling is conducted scientifically and carefully, it
gives more accuracy as compared to the census procedure.
Greater scope: There can be investigations where highly trained investigators
or specialized equipments are needed to collect the information.
Detailed Enquiry: Under sampling method, the number of units and the area of
study are small. So, it is possible to collect detail and in-depth information
about the population under study.
