Demerits
Difficult to achieve cent percent accuracy: The conclusions of sampling method
are based only on the results of a sample taken from the whole population.
Therefore, achieving a hundred percent degree of accuracy is not possible.
Lack of Representativeness of the Sample: The accuracy of conclusions of
sampling method depends upon whether the sample is representative of the
characteristics ofthe population.
Bias in the selection of sample: If the investigator is biased, then he might select
sample deliberately. In such cases, selected sample cannot be a representative
of the characteristics of population.
Lack of Specific or Specialized Knowledge: If the services of experts are not used
in the collection and analysis of sample data, the results of investigation are
likely to be unsatisfactory.
Not possible in case of heterogeneous population: In case of heterogeneous
population, any sample may not correctly reflect the characteristics of the
population. In this case, sampling is not advisable.
